1
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:23,820
This video demonstrates the donning and doffing of the following PPE.

2
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:30,780
Gown, gloves, disposable face mask, and face shield.

3
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:36,300
It also demonstrates removing the gown first and the glove second when doffing.

4
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:46,140
The first step is to remove personal items such as jewelry, watches, coats, jackets, cell phones,

5
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:52,540
pens, or additional bags, and place them in a location outside of the laboratory.

6
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:56,860
Then, tie back any long hair if present.

7
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:05,740
Next, gather your solid front wrap-around gown with knit cuffs, a single pair of gloves,

8
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:14,300
a disposable face mask, or an N95 respirator, and your disposable face shield.

9
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:20,620
The decision whether to use a disposable face mask or an N95 respirator

10
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:26,700
will depend on the laboratory site-specific and activity-specific risk assessment.

11
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:34,140
Please note, this scenario will demonstrate donning and doffing a disposable face mask.

12
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:42,110
Make sure you have the right size gown and gloves, and don't forget to visually inspect

13
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:50,750
all of your PPE for rips, tears, loose or missing straps, and replace any defective PPE you find.

14
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:58,830
Next, pull on the gown, fastening it securely behind your neck and back or side.

15
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:05,470
Do not tie the knot or fasten it so tightly that you cannot easily remove it later.

16
00:02:06,830 --> 00:02:10,350
Make sure the gown fits well to allow for easy movement.

17
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:13,470
Street clothing should not be exposed.

18
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:20,030
Next, put on your disposable face mask with the ear loops behind your ears,

19
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:23,230
ensuring a snug fit against your face.

20
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:30,910
With the index finger of both hands, press down on each side of the flexible nose piece

21
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:35,870
so that the top of the face mask fits snugly against your nose and cheeks.

22
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:39,710
Next, put on the disposable face shield.

23
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:46,590
Stretch to expand the elastic strap and place it behind your head with the foam resting

24
00:02:46,590 --> 00:02:53,550
just above your eyebrows. Adjust the strap so it fits snugly against your face.

25
00:02:54,430 --> 00:03:02,190
Face shields must cover your forehead, extend below your chin, and wrap around the sides of your face.

26
00:03:02,350 --> 00:03:09,790
Finally, put on your gloves. First, pull the gown's knit cuff down around the palm of your hand,

27
00:03:09,790 --> 00:03:17,870
and then pull the glove over, not under, the cuff. This helps ensure your sleeves won't slip out

28
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:22,430
and the knit cuff won't be exposed to hazardous materials during work.

29
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:28,830
Ensure, yet again, that there are no punctures or tears in the gloves prior to beginning work.

30
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:34,750
The following steps describe one method and sequence of doffing PPE.

31
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:41,710
Other methods and sequences may vary based on the laboratory site-specific and activity-specific risk

32
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:50,990
assessments, the procedures being conducted, and the PPE worn. The first step of doffing your PPE

33
00:03:51,630 --> 00:03:58,430
is removing your gown. To do this, untie the gown at your waist, grasp the gown's shoulders,

34
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:04,430
and pull the gown forward, releasing the neck closure. Pull the gown off of your shoulders

35
00:04:04,430 --> 00:04:11,230
and away from your body, rolling the gown inside out as you go. Before completely pulling off

36
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:17,230
the gown sleeves, carefully pull the gown sleeves from under your gloves and remove

37
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:24,750
your arms, leaving your gloves on. Roll the gown inside out into a bundle, taking care to

38
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:30,510
prevent the potentially contaminated outside of the gown from touching your street clothes.

39
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:38,350
Dispose of the bundle into the biohazard waste container. Next, slowly and gently remove your

40
00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:44,910
gloves. These steps describe one method of removing gloves to avoid contamination.

41
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:53,710
Other methods may be used based on your institutional preferences.

42
00:04:54,910 --> 00:05:02,270
To begin, make an L with your thumb and first finger. Then, place your fingers perpendicular

43
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:09,950
to your wrist and pinch. Next, pull the glove completely off. It should now be inside out.

44
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:16,510
Grab the inside out glove with your bare hand, the one the glove just came off of,

45
00:05:16,510 --> 00:05:24,270
and then pinch the other glove at the wrist. Then, pull the pinched glove up high and away

46
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:30,670
from the wrist. Pull the glove off, making sure the gloved hand is flat and don't touch

47
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:37,230
the outside of the contaminated glove with your clean hand. Last, discard the gloves

48
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:42,910
into the biohazard waste container. Remember, do not reuse the gloves.

49
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:51,150
Apply alcohol-based hand sanitizer with at least 60% ethanol or 70% isopropanol to your hands,

50
00:05:51,150 --> 00:05:55,710
wash your hands with soap and water, or don a new pair of gloves.

51
00:05:56,190 --> 00:06:03,230
Tilt your head slightly forward to take off your face shield. Grasp the straps above the ears

52
00:06:03,230 --> 00:06:09,470
and gently lift the face shield away from your face, taking care to avoid contaminating the

53
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:15,870
shield itself, which may be potentially contaminated. Then, discard the disposable

54
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:23,070
face shield in the biohazard waste container. To remove your disposable face mask, remove

55
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:29,230
the ear loops, taking care to avoid touching the potentially contaminated exterior surface

56
00:06:29,230 --> 00:06:35,710
of the face mask. Pull the mask away from your face and dispose of it in the biohazard

57
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:44,510
waste container. Last, wash your hands with soap and water. Lather the backs of your hands,

58
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:50,670
between your fingers and under your nails, and scrub for at least 20 seconds.

59
00:06:52,510 --> 00:06:57,950
Washing your hands with soap and water is the best method. However, if soap and water are

60
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:06,670
unavailable, an alcohol-based hand sanitizer containing at least 60% ethanol or 70% isopropanol

61
00:07:06,670 --> 00:07:11,390
can be used as a temporary solution until soap and water are available.

62
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:18,590
Additional considerations. Clothed-toed shoes with solid and impermeable uppers

63
00:07:18,590 --> 00:07:25,310
should be worn in the laboratory. PPE will vary based on a laboratory site-specific and

64
00:07:25,310 --> 00:07:31,790
activity-specific risk assessment. Donning and doffing areas should be physically separated

65
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:36,830
from each other to avoid contamination of clean PPE and personal belongings

66
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:43,710
with potentially contaminated PPE. Donning and doffing procedures vary per institution.

67
00:07:44,350 --> 00:07:51,230
Follow institutional policies and procedures. For additional training and workforce development

68
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:59,070
resources, please visit cdc.gov slash lab training and click on the job aids button.
